  "name": "Yawulyu (Warlpiri women's ceremonial song)",
  "family": "global",
  "lineage": "Women's ceremonial song and dance of the Warlpiri of the Tanami Desert, held by senior women at Yuendumu, Lajamanu and neighbouring communities, in which song series follow the Jukurrpa (Dreaming) tracks of particular country and are performed with body painting and dance. Senior Yuendumu women documented their repertoire with linguists and musicologists in the book-and-audio publication Yurntumu-wardingki juju-ngaliya-kurlangu yawulyu (Batchelor Press, 2017).",
